[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3870794385","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116086#issuecomment-3870794385","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116086","id":3870794385,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mt6KR","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T10:22:35Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T10:22:35Z","body":"This is expected behavior. Only language constructs like the `and`, `or`, and ternary operators can have short-circuit behavior. `Dictionary.get()` is a regular method, albeit a built-in one. Godot/GDScript doesn't have lazy evaluation, there's no way to mark a method argument as conditionally and lazily evaluated. To call a function, GDScript must first evaluate its arguments.\n\nYou can use `Dictionary.has()` to first check if a key exists in a dictionary:\n\n```gdscript\nfunc print_vehicle_qty() -> void:\n    var quantity = my_dict.get(\"Car\") if my_dict.has(\"Car\") else my_function(3)\n    print(\"Car quantity: \", quantity)\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3870794385/reactions","total_count":6,"+1":6,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3873466474","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116086#issuecomment-3873466474","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116086","id":3873466474,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7m4Ghq","user":{"login":"Teufelauto","id":110637430,"node_id":"U_kgDOBpgxdg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/110637430?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Teufelauto","html_url":"https://github.com/Teufelauto","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Teufelauto/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Teufelauto/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Teufelauto/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Teufelauto/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Teufelauto/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Teufelauto/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Teufelauto/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Teufelauto/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Teufelauto/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T19:32:16Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T19:32:16Z","body":"@dalexeev  Thank you for the clarification, and your time spent crafting a response. I will use the .has() method as suggested.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3873466474/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3874976189","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116086#issuecomment-3874976189","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116086","id":3874976189,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7m93G9","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-10T02:32:49Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T02:32:49Z","body":"I suppose that we should update the docs with this? If so, I'll create a PR.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3874976189/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3876270869","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116086#issuecomment-3876270869","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116086","id":3876270869,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7nCzMV","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-10T08:59:18Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T08:59:18Z","body":"> I suppose that we should update the docs with this? If so, I'll create a PR.\n\nWe could mention this in the `Dictionary.get()` documentation. Something like \"If the `default` argument is computationally expensive or has unwanted side effects, consider using the `has()` method instead.\".\n\nTechnically, users should understand that this applies to all calls, so we should only mention it in the GDScript Reference. But since users don't always carefully read the general documentation, it seems fine to me to add a mention for a few specific methods where this error is most likely. An inexperienced or inattentive user might easily miss the difference between `dict.get(\"key\", 1)` and `dict.get(\"key\", some_method())`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3876270869/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]